From: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com>
Sent: Monday, February 3, 2025 9:46 AM
To: BLISS Logan * OPRD <Logan.BLISS@oprd.oregon.gov>
Subject: Re: Gate

Good morning, Logan.

I appreciate the adaptation.

Would you like me to take on the gate duties as specified? I am happy to do=
 it - this was not a ploy on my part. It feels like a natural part of my rh=
ythm here.

I assume you're still evaluating me (this is fine) and maybe I'll hear abou=
t October before you've filled it? I would sincerely like to come back then=
.

Regarding next year, I ask that you consider me for this spot and this posi=
tion from February through April. I'd like to be here through the end of th=
e dune season if you're amenable. (Again, understand you are still evaluati=
ng me. Also understand if you have others for those months and would need t=
o put me in different roles, I believe I'm open to that.)

Regarding my current job - first day, I forgot to write anything on the env=
elope. Second day, I did but I couldn't find anything in the binder telling=
 me what to write there. I don't think I overlooked it but perhaps I did. I=
 looked pretty hard though.

Definitely feeling the position out and developing a rhythm for it. See you=
 at orientation.


Sam

